@startuml
' Evidence: Laplace-Engine/src/db.c SHA256 bba138c55e319e63598cd8c6640d0de5428975c5b37991e8439823efea5d17c7
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
title Modular Engine — recover prepared transaction parts
start

:Begin two recovery rounds;
while (Another recovery round?) is (yes)
 :Query laplace-prefixed prepared transactions in current database;
 :Only consider parts older than two minutes; order by numeric part;
 if (Query fails?) then (yes)
  :Return false;
  stop
 endif
 while (More returned parts?) is (yes)
  if (First round and part is not zero?) then (yes)
   :Skip until next round;
  else (eligible)
   if (Part zero or coordinator status committed?) then (yes)
    :COMMIT PREPARED;
   elseif (Coordinator status aborted?) then (yes)
    :ROLLBACK PREPARED;
   else (other status)
    :Leave part unresolved for now;
   endif
   if (Issued statement fails?) then (yes)
    :Return false;
    stop
   endif
  endif
 endwhile (no)
endwhile (no)
:Return true;

stop
footer
Source-reviewed orchestration. Nested semantics remain open; no runtime acceptance
claimed. Part zero is prepared last and committed first by load/merge. Recovery commits a
prepared part zero, then follows its transaction status for other parts. The two-minute
eligibility threshold is literal source policy. Runtime crash-recovery behavior is not
tested by this atlas.
end footer

@enduml
